# Commits that `git blame` should look THROUGH, because their content is mechanical.
#
# Why this file exists: a repo-wide `cargo fmt` rewrites every file, which destroys
# blame (every line is suddenly authored by the formatter) and pollutes the churn
# measurement that ADR-0042 D10 now ranks splits by. Black's migration guide has a
# section for exactly this, "Avoiding ruining git blame", and Blender, GitLab and gpdb
# all use the mechanism. GitHub's blame view reads this file by default; for local use,
# `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs` (git >= 2.23).
#
# So the formatting change is a single commit whose SHA goes below, and blame and churn
# both see through it. That removes the only reason `cargo fmt` was being deferred.
#
# FORMAT: one full 40-character SHA per line, comments with `#`. Short SHAs are not
# accepted by git and fail silently, which would be the usual defect in this repository.
#
